{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy to mcp_servers.json (gitignored) or set the same JSON in the",
    "MCP_SERVERS environment variable, which takes precedence.",
    "",
    "Only the streamable-HTTP transport is supported. stdio servers are not:",
    "each one is a node/python subprocess costing 50-150 MB against a 1 GB box",
    "already running two workers, and spawning processes on the model's behalf",
    "is what isolation.py exists to contain.",
    "",
    "`tier` is the governor risk tier and the operator's call, not the",
    "server's. Omit it and the server is treated as EXTERNAL, meaning every",
    "call from an unattended run parks for approval. Set it to `read` only",
    "for servers that genuinely cannot change anything.",
    "",
    "mcp_call is owner-only regardless of tier: the tier bounds how far an",
    "effect reaches, not who may invoke it."
  ],

  "servers": {
    "docs": {
      "url": "https://example.com/mcp",
      "tier": "read",
      "enabled": false
    },
    "deploy": {
      "url": "https://example.com/deploy/mcp",
      "headers": {"Authorization": "Bearer ${put-a-real-token-here}"},
      "tier": "external",
      "timeout": 120,
      "enabled": false
    }
  }
}
